    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the single driveway entrance so responders can confirm the correct property at night or in low visibility.\n• Keep the driveway clear of parked vehicles to allow emergency apparatus to reach both structures without obstruction.\n• Trim vegetation along both sides of the driveway so responding vehicles can pass without obstruction.\n• Cut back dense vegetation that narrows or blocks side access routes between and around the structures.\n• Mark or number both structures visibly from the driveway so responders can immediately identify which structure they are approaching.\n• Keep a clear path between the two structures so responders can move between them on foot without pushing through vegetation.\n• Keep gates or barriers on side access routes unlocked or equipped with a lockbox so responders are not delayed reaching the rear of the property.\n• Keep the area around the water feature clear so responders working near it are not at risk of an undetected drop-off or edge hazard.\n• Identify and maintain at least one open staging area, such as the parking area or open lawn, that can accommodate an emergency vehicle or crew without blocking the access route."
