    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs and low-hanging branches that are directly touching or within a few feet of the house on all sides.\n• Remove tall grass growing close to the base of the house and any attached or nearby structures.\n• Cut or mow the tall grass area down before it dries out seasonally.\n• Thin trees in the tree clusters nearest to the house to create gaps between the canopies.\n• Remove low branches from scattered trees near the house so flames cannot climb from the ground into the tree tops.\n• Clear dead plant material, fallen branches, and leaf litter from beneath the dense vegetation area closest to the house.\n• Thin the brush area to break up the continuous mass of vegetation leading toward the house.\n• Mow or cut the grass cover areas near the house and any outbuildings regularly during dry periods.\n• Separate the mixed vegetation from the sides of the house by clearing a bare or short-mowed strip directly against the foundation.\n• Keep all access routes clear of overhanging branches and overgrown vegetation along the edges.\n• Maintain enough clearance on each access route so emergency vehicles can pass without obstruction from both sides.\n• Remove any vegetation or debris that has grown into or over the edges of the driveway or secondary access paths."
